File Handling in C
This repository contains C programming exercises focused on file handling, data storage, and data retrieval. The activities explore working with text files, binary files, structures, and file operations
 Library Book Records (Text File)

A program that allows a librarian to enter borrowed book titles and store them in a text file named "borrowed_books.txt".

The program:

- Accepts book titles from the user.
- Stores book titles in a text file.
- Preserves existing records when new titles are added.
- Displays a confirmation message when a book title is successfully stored.

Q2. Student Examination Records (Binary File)

A program that stores student examination results in a binary file named "results.dat".

Each record contains:

- Student name
- Registration number
- Total marks

The program:

- Defines a structure to store student information.
- Reads student records from the binary file.
- Displays each student's name and marks on the screen.

Q3. Sales Transaction Records (Text File)

A program that reads daily sales transactions from a text file named "sales.txt".

The program:

- Reads all sales transactions stored in the file.
- Calculates the total sales for the day.
- Displays the total sales amount.
- Ensures the file is properly closed after reading.

